; ================================================================
; scene_3d.scr
; FULL SCENE = PANEL + RAILS + RAIL-GUIDED ROBOT, in one drawing.
; REE598 GRADUATION PROJECT  -  DATE 2026-06-13   UNITS MM
;
; This script NESTS the two component scripts via the SCRIPT command,
; so the carriage ends up sitting on the rails in a single drawing.
; Order: infrastructure first (panel + rails), then the robot on top.
;
; HOW TO RUN (AutoCAD 2026):
;   1. Put scene_3d.scr, rail_and_panel_3d.scr and pvbot_3d_assembly.scr
;      in the SAME folder.
;   2. New drawing from acadiso.dwt (metric, mm).
;   3. SCRIPT -> pick scene_3d.scr.
;   4. ZOOM E, then -VIEW SWISO for the isometric.
;
; If nested SCRIPT calls are blocked by your security settings, just run
; the two component scripts in sequence by hand (rail_and_panel_3d.scr
; first, then pvbot_3d_assembly.scr) - the result is identical.
; ================================================================
FILEDIA 0
EXPERT 5

; ---- infrastructure: PV panel, posts, rails, rack, end stops ----
SCRIPT rail_and_panel_3d.scr

; ---- the rail-guided carriage robot, dropped onto the rails ----
SCRIPT pvbot_3d_assembly.scr

; ---- final framing ----
ZOOM
E
-VIEW SWISO
VSCURRENT
R
ZOOM
E
EXPERT 0
FILEDIA 1
; ---------------- end scene_3d.scr ----------------
